                      (    forth6809.asm):07949                                  ; elsewhere in this file), so BPL was always
                      (    forth6809.asm):07950                                  ; testing CLR's result, not n1's actual sign.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07951                                  ; BPL always branched, meaning n1 was NEVER
                      (    forth6809.asm):07952                                  ; negated even when genuinely negative - found
                      (    forth6809.asm):07953                                  ; via MAME: TSTMSTAR's two returned values
                      (    forth6809.asm):07954                                  ; came back wrong, which turned out to be
                      (    forth6809.asm):07955                                  ; this, not a push-order swap in the test
                      (    forth6809.asm):07956                                  ; itself. FMSLASHMOD/SMSLASHREM already do
                      (    forth6809.asm):07957                                  ; this correctly (explicit TST PRODHI between
                      (    forth6809.asm):07958                                  ; their own CLR calls and the branch) - MSTAR
